
<p><a href="https://daringfireball.net/2026/08/apple_testflight_list_sort_order">I wrote two weeks ago</a> about how the v4.3.0 update to TestFlight (released on July 21) broke the sort order for apps in the sidebar. Apple yesterday released v4.3.1, with these helpful release notes:</p>

<blockquote>
  <p>This update includes stability improvements and bug fixes.</p>
</blockquote>

<p>One of the weirdest parts about this sort-order bug is that <a href="https://daringfireball.net/linked/2026/08/24/more-on-testflights-screwy-sort-order">it only affected some people</a>. I was obviously one of them; <a href="https://mastodon.social/@siracusa/117135117635246786">so was John Siracusa</a>. For both of us, yesterday’s v4.3.1 update fixes the bug.</p>

